From: tanojericko <115430549+tanojericko@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] 1300D: don't give the audio gain semaphore before it exists

CRASH00.LOG on a Rebel T6 (M-Film 0.2.1):
  ASSERT: 0 at SystemIF::KerSem.c:354, PropMgr
The stack goes through global_property_handler (blx to a handler) into
give_semaphore. The handler is PROP_MVR_REC_START in audio-common.c:
enable_recording() gives gain.sem, which is the placeholder (void*)1 until
my_sounddev_task (audio-ak.c) creates the real semaphore. If the property
fires first, Canon asserts in PropMgr, the property task dies and the GUI
freezes while the shutter still works.
---
diff --git a/src/audio-common.c b/src/audio-common.c
index 9135844..965599d 100755
--- a/src/audio-common.c
+++ b/src/audio-common.c
@@ -81,6 +81,16 @@ static struct gain_struct gain = {
     .sem                    = (void*) 1,
 };
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_1300D
+/* gain.sem is a placeholder (1) until my_sounddev_task (audio-ak.c) creates
+ * the real semaphore. On the 1300D, PROP_MVR_REC_START can fire before that,
+ * and give_semaphore(1) asserts in Canon's KerSem.c inside PropMgr: the
+ * property task dies and the GUI freezes (shutter still works). */
+#define give_gain_sem() do { if ((uintptr_t) gain.sem > 1) give_semaphore( gain.sem ); } while (0)
+#else
+#define give_gain_sem() give_semaphore( gain.sem )
+#endif
+
 
 static CONFIG_VAR_CHANGE_FUNC(lovl_on_change)
 {
@@ -1061,7 +1071,7 @@ enable_recording(int mode)
             #if defined(CONFIG_600D) || defined(CONFIG_7D)
             audio_configure(1);
             #else
-            give_semaphore( gain.sem );
+            give_gain_sem();
             #endif
             break;
         case 1:
@@ -1076,7 +1086,7 @@ enable_recording(int mode)
 // to be called from some other tasks that may mess with audio 
 static void audio_force_reconfigure() 
 {
-    give_semaphore( gain.sem ); 
+    give_gain_sem();
 }
 
 static void
